From: Prithwiraj Samanta <prskid1000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 06:59:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] telecode: component slots on instance-swap properties

A slot is a named area of a component that each instance fills with its own
content. .fig derives instance children from the main component, so slots are
built on what it persists - the instance-swap property: telecode_slot_create
moves a frame's children into a default-content component (page section
"Slot content"), replaces the frame by an exposed instance of it and marks it
telecode/slot; telecode_slot_fill gives one instance its own content (Design
JSX, moved layers or an existing component); telecode_slot_reset restores the
default; telecode_slot_list reads them. Unused content components telecode
made are removed. The Slot content section is not a slide.
